From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:07:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Pass Rust 1.99.1 macOS links and lints under fatal warnings

Upstream builds with Rust 1.99.1 (#61205), which files ld's "ignoring
duplicate libraries: '-lSystem'" message under the allow-by-default
linker_info lint, so macOS links of codex-code-mode-host pass under the
workspace's denied linker_messages lint.

The release codex binary's __eh_frame section exceeds the 16 MB that
compact unwind's DWARF offsets can reach, and ld says so on stderr, which
fails the link. Link Apple targets through scripts/apple-linker.sh, which
drops that one exact notice and passes every other linker message through.

Clippy's redundant_field_names fires inside thiserror 2.0.18's expansion of
`#[from] source`, and double_must_use fires on the boxed futures that
async-trait 0.1.89 returns from tonic's generated traits. Move thiserror and
thiserror-impl to 2.0.21 and async-trait to 0.1.92, which trigger neither.

Since Rust 1.97, linker_messages warns by default but ignores -D warnings,
so the workspace comment gives that as the reason for denying it.
---
 codex-rs/.cargo/config.toml      |   8 ++
 codex-rs/Cargo.lock              | 188 +++++++++++++++----------------
 codex-rs/Cargo.toml              |   2 +-
 codex-rs/scripts/apple-linker.sh |  25 ++++
 4 files changed, 128 insertions(+), 95 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 codex-rs/scripts/apple-linker.sh

diff --git a/codex-rs/.cargo/config.toml b/codex-rs/.cargo/config.toml
index 2de645c21e..91c41b6882 100644
--- a/codex-rs/.cargo/config.toml
+++ b/codex-rs/.cargo/config.toml
@@ -19,3 +19,11 @@ rustflags = ["-C", "link-arg=/STACK:8388608", "-C", "link-arg=/arm64hazardfree"]
 
 [target.'cfg(all(windows, target_env = "gnu"))']
 rustflags = ["-C", "link-arg=-Wl,--stack,8388608"]
+
+# ld reports that the codex binary's __eh_frame section exceeds compact unwind's 16 MB reach, which the denied
+# linker_messages lint would turn into a build failure; the wrapper drops only that notice.
+[target.aarch64-apple-darwin]
+linker = "scripts/apple-linker.sh"
+
+[target.x86_64-apple-darwin]
+linker = "scripts/apple-linker.sh"
